  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Ember sizes, spark sprays and the singe marks vary per cast. The three toss times (0.09 s apart), arcs and pop times stay fixed so the hit rhythm is the same every cast: three hits about 0.1 s apart."
  },
  "director_notes": "A light basic attack, the small cousin of Inferno Burst. Choices: (1) nearly no wind-up (90 ms kindle, 40 ms flick) so it fires the moment it's pressed; (2) three small embers, each its own orb flying in its own travel beat, launched about 0.09 s apart on three different arcs (a 12 px skim, a 55 px lob, a 30 px middle) so the volley reads as three shots from the side and 3/4 instead of one blob; (3) three small pops (separate impact beats with their own sparks), a stacking burn and a small singe that outlives the spell. Hero view is 3/4, where the arcs separate. Sound: a high-pitched ignite per ember, a light impact per pop, a quiet sizzle tail. A game can treat each pop as its own hit for damage numbers."
}
